  "community-highway-truck-rescue": Object.freeze({"sourcePromptAvailable":true,"sourceAuditStatus":"verified-2026-11-05","sourceTitle":"Highway Truck Rescue","sourceMediaId":"cb12a521-241e-458e-bc71-73c6781458a0","prompt":"MODE: Motion Transfer\nSOURCE: Reference video (white truck losing balance, hero truck entering and stabilizing it)\nDURATION / FORMAT: 10 seconds, 9:16 vertical, one continuous shot, realistic cinematic commercial style, rear tracking camera exactly as in source video — no cuts.\nREFERENCE MAPPING:\nImage 1 (White Truck Character Sheet) → the truck already present in the source footage from 00:00. Preserve exact truck model, white cab, light-gray canvas, \"YOUR BUSINESS\" wordmark centered on rear canvas in dark navy, clean sans-serif, no background panel.\nImage 3 (unctrl Hero Truck Character Sheet) → the truck entering from the right at ~00:04. Preserve exact truck model, matte black full body, unctrl white wordmark centered on rear canvas, no background box.\nImage 2 (Storyboard) → use only for timing/action reference (frames 01–10), not for branding.\nACTION TIMELINE (from storyboard, keep exact pacing):\n00:00–00:03: White truck (Image 1) drives normally on highway, then begins tilting toward the right, tilt increasing, cargo body descending — physically grounded, motion-blur consistent with speed.\n00:04: unctrl hero truck (Image 3) enters frame from the right, positions itself beside the white truck.\n00:05–00:06: Hero truck closes the gap, gently supports/leans into the white truck's cargo body, rotation stops.\n00:07: Cargo-to-cargo metal contact, rotation fully arrested.\n00:08–00:09: White truck gradually recovers to upright position.\n00:09–00:10: Both trucks upright, aligned, driving forward together in final composition.\nPRESERVE: highway environment, city skyline and mountain backdrop, daylight lighting, rear 3/4 tracking camera angle and movement, road markings, motion blur, truck proportions and structure exactly as in each character sheet, physics of the tilt-and-recover motion.\nDO NOT CHANGE: truck models/proportions, camera framing, road/environment, number of vehicles. Do not place any logo anywhere except the rear canvas of each truck. Do not alter or duplicate the logos.\nSOUND DESIGN (SFX + Music):\nContinuous low diesel engine rumble and tire-on-asphalt hum under the whole shot, rising slightly in pitch as the white truck tilts (tension cue).\nSubtle metallic creak/groan as the white truck's cargo leans (00:01–00:03).\nLow string tension/rising drone building from 00:00 to 00:03 (suspense).\nA brief musical \"arrival\" hit / low brass swell exactly at 00:04 when the unctrl hero truck enters frame — this is the hero moment.\nSoft metal-to-metal clunk/thud sound effect at the contact point (00:06–00:07), not harsh or crash-like, more of a supportive \"catch\" sound.\nMusic shifts from tense to uplifting: a rising orchestral/cinematic swell with light percussion from 00:07 to 00:10, resolving into a confident, steady rhythmic pulse as both trucks drive forward together in the final frame — a triumphant, \"rescue accomplished\" tone.\nWind whoosh/doppler effect on both trucks throughout, consistent with highway speed.\nNEGATIVE PROMPT: no extra logos, no rebranding elsewhere on the trucks, no truck redesign or proportion distortion, no jump cuts, no camera shake/glitches, no unrealistic physics, no additional vehicles, no text overlays."}),
