  "community-bathroom-duo": Object.freeze({"sourcePromptAvailable":true,"sourceAuditStatus":"verified-2026-11-05","sourceTitle":"Bathroom Duo","sourceMediaId":"43ca455c-4037-4355-b028-d1f03cf5288a","prompt":"SEEDANCE — STRICT CHARACTER IDENTITY LOCK + MOTION & AUDIO TRANSFER\n\nCreate a high-quality Pixar-style 3D animated video using the uploaded character and location references.\n\nCRITICAL: STRICT REFERENCE SEPARATION\n\n1. CHARACTERS — ABSOLUTE IDENTITY LOCK\n\nUse ONLY the characters from the uploaded character reference images.\n\nPreserve their exact facial features, eye shapes, eye colors, hairstyles, body proportions, clothing, skin tones, and original 3D cartoon appearance.\n\nDo NOT redraw, redesign, reinterpret, regenerate, or modify the characters.\n\nThey must remain visually identical to their reference images throughout the entire video, including during facial expressions and movement.\n\n2. ORIGINAL VIDEO — MOTION AND AUDIO ONLY\n\nUse the original video EXCLUSIVELY to transfer:\n\n* Exact facial expressions and lip movements.\n* Exact body movements, gestures, and actions.\n* Exact head movements and eye direction.\n* Exact timing, rhythm, and synchronization.\n* Original audio, sound effects, and timing.\n\nReproduce the original performance frame by frame as closely as possible.\n\nDo NOT transfer the original actors’ faces, appearance, clothing, body proportions, or visual style.\n\n3. LOCATION — STRICT REFERENCE LOCK\n\nUse ONLY the uploaded bathroom location reference.\n\nPreserve its layout, furniture, colors, lighting, and Pixar-style 3D appearance.\n\nDo NOT copy or recreate the background from the original video.\n\n4. CAMERA AND ANIMATION\n\nMatch the original video’s camera framing, movement timing, and action sequence while keeping our characters and location unchanged.\n\nMaintain smooth, natural animation and precise synchronization with the original audio.\n\nFINAL PRIORITY:\n\nOur exact characters + our exact location + original video’s facial expressions, movements, actions, timing, and audio.\n\nONLY TRANSFER THE PERFORMANCE. NEVER TRANSFER OR RECREATE THE ORIGINAL VIDEO’S VISUAL IDENTITY."}),
