  "community-winter-streetwear-film": Object.freeze({"sourcePromptAvailable":true,"sourceAuditStatus":"verified-2026-11-05","sourceTitle":"Winter Streetwear Film","sourceMediaId":"5783687b-2388-4c81-8c90-c58589ba5b75","prompt":"GENJITSU LITE — YOU'RE JACKPOT | CINEMATIC WINTER CAMPAIGN\nPROJECT: Ultra-photorealistic luxury streetwear fashion film.\nDURATION: Approximately 14 seconds.\nFORMAT: 9:16 vertical, cinematic 24fps aesthetic.\nPRIMARY OBJECTIVE\nRecreate the cinematic atmosphere, editing rhythm, visual composition, camera language, environmental motion, and shot progression of the supplied original reference video, replacing its original fashion garments and models with the exact IKONIK \"You're Jackpot\" hoodie campaign subjects shown in Reference Images 1–8.\nThe result must look like a real high-budget winter fashion commercial, professionally photographed on location, never like AI-generated animation.\nABSOLUTE REFERENCE PRIORITY\nOriginal video: Primary reference for cinematography, pacing, camera angles, shot transitions, environmental movement, and visual atmosphere.\nImages 1–2: Full-body female and male rear-view compositions.\nImages 3–4: Exact hoodie back graphics, proportions, and close-up framing.\nImages 5–6: Male and female facial appearance, front hoodie details, and hood-up portraits.\nImages 7–8: Exact sleeve shapes, fabric texture, cuffs, hands, and garment construction.\nPreserve each model's identity, hairstyle, body proportions, clothing color, and original garment design consistently throughout the entire video.\nENVIRONMENT AND CINEMATOGRAPHY\nA freezing urban street at night.\nMassive cold grey architectural wall with visible horizontal and vertical panel divisions. A bright overhead streetlight illuminates the snow. Wet black asphalt reflects the surrounding light.\nA dark parking meter stands near the central model. Pedestrians in winter clothing pass through the background, occasionally appearing motion-blurred. Dark vehicles move naturally across the foreground.\nRealistic snowfall with different particle sizes, speeds, and depths. Occasional visible condensation from cold breath.\nColor grading: desaturated steel blue, cold cyan-grey highlights, deep charcoal shadows, restrained contrast, natural skin tones.\nCamera aesthetic: ARRI ALEXA 35, cinematic 35mm and 50mm spherical lenses, realistic optical depth of field, subtle organic film grain, natural motion blur, professional exposure, soft highlight roll-off.\nNo excessive camera movement, artificial glow, unrealistic contrast, or synthetic textures.\nCINEMATIC SHOT SEQUENCE\nSHOT 01 — WHITE HOODIE ESTABLISHING\nBegin with a wide, symmetrical rear view of the female model wearing the exact oversized white hoodie and matching white baggy sweatpants from Image 1.\nShe stands motionless beneath the overhead streetlight.\nThe back graphic is visible.\nSnow falls naturally. A pedestrian walks past in the background while a dark car briefly crosses the foreground.\nCamera remains stable with an almost imperceptible slow push-in.\nSHOT 02 — WHITE HOODIE PRODUCT DETAIL\nTransition to a tighter rear view matching Image 4.\nEmphasize the exact black calligraphic \"You're Jackpot\" lettering, two translucent blue dice, decorative symbol, \"Ikonik Project\" signature, and the smaller bottom sentence.\nMaintain the exact graphic scale, alignment, typography, spacing, and positioning.\nThe fabric moves almost imperceptibly with natural breathing.\nSnow settles gently on the shoulders and hood.\nSHOT 03 — BLACK HOODIE ESTABLISHING\nCut to the male model from Image 2.\nHe stands facing away from the camera in the exact same winter environment.\nHe wears the oversized black hoodie and wide black trousers.\nHis posture is relaxed, strong, and still.\nThe exact back print remains clearly visible.\nBackground pedestrians and passing vehicles create subtle urban movement.\nSHOT 04 — BLACK HOODIE BACK PRINT CLOSE-UP\nA cinematic medium-close rear shot matching Image 3.\nThe black hoodie fills most of the frame.\nPreserve the exact cream-colored calligraphic lettering, two blue translucent dice, ornamental detail, signature, and small bottom text.\nShow natural fabric texture, realistic seams, snow accumulation, and dimensional folds.\nUse a very slow controlled camera push-in.\nThe print remains perfectly attached to the garment surface without warping, drifting, or changing.\nSHOT 05 — BLACK HOODIE FRONT PORTRAIT\nCut to the male model from Image 5.\nHis hood is raised.\nHe faces the camera directly with a cold, serious, expressionless gaze.\nSubtle breath vapor escapes from his mouth.\nHis face remains anatomically realistic, with visible pores, natural skin texture, and accurate facial proportions.\nThe front chest print remains exactly as shown in Image 5.\nMinimal natural head movement. No exaggerated facial expressions.\nSHOT 06 — WHITE HOODIE FRONT PORTRAIT\nCut to the female model from Image 6.\nHer white hood is raised.\nShe maintains intense, direct eye contact with the camera.\nPreserve her exact facial features, freckles, hairstyle, earrings, and natural skin texture.\nCold breath vapor drifts briefly in front of her.\nThe small front chest graphic retains its exact original size, typography, and placement.\nCamera remains steady.\nSHOT 07 — BLACK FABRIC DETAIL\nMacro fashion shot matching Image 7.\nShow the black oversized sleeve, ribbed cuff, hand, and kangaroo pocket.\nThe hand makes a very small, natural movement.\nFine snow particles collect on the fabric and gradually melt.\nPreserve realistic cotton texture, stitching, garment weight, and folds.\nSHOT 08 — WHITE FABRIC DETAIL\nMacro fashion shot matching Image 8.\nFocus on the white oversized sleeve, cuff, partially visible hand, and fabric surface.\nThe hand relaxes naturally with subtle finger movement.\nSnowflakes fall across the foreground and settle on the material.\nMaintain authentic textile texture and realistic lighting.\nPRINT FIDELITY — CRITICAL\nAll hoodie graphics are fixed, physical prints on real garments.\nDo not redraw, reinterpret, regenerate, simplify, replace, translate, or stylize any lettering, dice, decorative symbols, or small text.\nPreserve the exact original typography, character shapes, letter spacing, line breaks, relative proportions, print dimensions, print colors, and positioning.\nThe two blue dice must retain their exact original geometry, transparency, orientation, perspective, and white dot arrangement.\nGraphics must follow natural fabric folds without changing their underlying design.\nNo flickering typography, shifting graphics, missing letters, duplicated dice, or inconsistent print placement between shots.\nPHYSICAL REALISM\nAll human motion must follow natural anatomy and gravity.\nMaintain consistent identities and body proportions across all shots.\nSnowfall, breath condensation, moving vehicles, pedestrians, fabric movement, and camera motion must interact naturally with the environment.\nRealistic temporal consistency between consecutive frames.\nNo artificial slow-motion gestures, excessive movement, face morphing, rubber-like fabric, plastic skin, or floating objects.\nFINAL ART DIRECTION\nCold. Minimal. Mysterious. Rebellious. Sophisticated.\nHigh-end European streetwear campaign meets cinematic winter street photography.\nAuthentic real-world fashion filmmaking.\nNatural imperfections, believable atmosphere, restrained camera motion, realistic lighting, and highly detailed garments.\nNo subtitles, no watermarks, no unrelated logos, no original brand end card.\nFINAL RESULT: A seamless, photorealistic IKONIK \"You're Jackpot\" winter campaign film that feels genuinely captured by a professional cinematography crew."}),
