  "community-reptilian-fridge-raid": Object.freeze({"sourcePromptAvailable":true,"sourceAuditStatus":"verified-2026-11-05","sourceTitle":"Reptilian Fridge Raid","sourceMediaId":"43a67555-122b-46e1-8394-3d2275c7a21b","prompt":"Use <<<video_1>>> as the exact motion, timing, framing, camera angle, and performance reference.\nUse <<<image_1>>> as the exact character identity reference for Kaiman.\n\nReplace the person in the source video with a believable ultra-photorealistic live-action Kaiman from Dorohedoro, while preserving the original action and meme structure of the video.\n\nKaiman stands outside an open refrigerator and eats directly from a large rectangular aluminum food tray with a spoon, exactly matching the behavior in <<<video_1>>>. He repeatedly scoops food quickly, eats greedily, and keeps digging back into the tray. The tray gradually becomes more empty, with visible scrape marks where the spoon removes the food. Keep the action funny, shameless, gluttonous, and slightly feral, just like a late-night fridge raid.\n\nPreserve the original refrigerator POV from inside the fridge. Preserve the casual meme realism, static camera feeling, and the overall blocking from the source video.\n\nKaiman must look like a real live-action creature-performance version of the character:\ngreen reptilian head, natural realistic scales with subtle organic shine, short spikes on top of the head, round pale eyes, red cross-like markings around both eyes, sharp visible teeth, strong thick neck, dark hooded jacket with the signature pale rib-like chest straps, rugged practical clothing, believable physical presence.\nHe must feel like a real photographed character, not a cartoon or CGI mascot.\n\nImportant: keep the source video action almost unchanged. The main change is only the character swap into Kaiman.\nMaintain the spoon-eating action, the tray in foreground, the open-fridge perspective, and the comedic greedy pacing.\n\nStyle: ultra-photorealistic live-action, practical creature suit realism, grounded textures, real food, real spoon, real fridge interior, believable lighting.\nLighting: cold refrigerator light from inside the fridge, slightly darker room outside.\nCamera: static fridge POV, no cinematic camera moves.\n\nNEGATIVE:\nno anime look, no cartoon, no stylized illustration, no plastic creature, no toy-like skin, no exaggerated CGI, no human face, no wrong costume, no extra limbs, no fantasy battle, no heroic posing, no dramatic action scene, no surreal transformations, no spoon disappearing, no tray disappearing"}),
